<figure class="tgs-diagram" data-diagram-id="service-transformation-office-gate-sequence" aria-labelledby="tgs-title" aria-describedby="tgs-caption tgs-note">
  <div class="tgs-header">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow text-accent">Route artifact · service and change</p>
      <h2 id="tgs-title" class="mt-5 max-w-3xl font-display text-3xl font-medium tracking-[-0.05em] md:text-4xl">A change cadence with a gate at every promise.</h2>
      <p id="tgs-caption" class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/70">Programs move safely when the portfolio, service owner, delivery team, and people affected by the change can see the next decision. Gates are evidence reviews, not ceremony.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="tgs-code" aria-hidden="true">CHANGE / SERVICE<br /><span>GATE SEQUENCE</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tgs-visual" role="img" aria-label="Five change gates progress from mandate to service learning: align, shape, release, stabilize, learn." tabindex="0">
    <div class="tgs-line" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <ol class="tgs-gates">
      <li><span>Mandate</span><strong>Align</strong><small>outcome · owner</small></li>
      <li><span>Portfolio</span><strong>Shape</strong><small>backlog · risk</small></li>
      <li><span>Evidence</span><strong>Release</strong><small>approval · control</small></li>
      <li><span>Service</span><strong>Stabilize</strong><small>support · continuity</small></li>
      <li><span>Outcome</span><strong>Learn</strong><small>signal · next move</small></li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <ol class="tgs-evidence" aria-label="Evidence required at each change gate" tabindex="0">
    <li><span class="tgs-index">Align</span><h3>Make the outcome govern the backlog.</h3><p>Portfolio sponsors agree the service promise, boundary, decision owner, and measures that make the work worth doing.</p><strong>Gate evidence · mandate and dependency map</strong></li>
    <li><span class="tgs-index">Shape</span><h3>Make delivery small enough to learn.</h3><p>Teams slice the work, expose risk, and choose an agile or lean delivery rhythm that fits the service and its constraints.</p><strong>Gate evidence · release hypothesis</strong></li>
    <li><span class="tgs-index">Release</span><h3>Change the service with a visible decision.</h3><p>Test results, readiness, communications, rollback, and the accountable approver travel together through the change window.</p><strong>Gate evidence · release record</strong></li>
    <li><span class="tgs-index">Stabilize</span><h3>Protect continuity after the launch.</h3><p>Support teams own the new normal, incidents and requests are observable, and exceptions have a route back to the program.</p><strong>Gate evidence · service transition note</strong></li>
    <li><span class="tgs-index">Learn</span><h3>Turn the result into the next portfolio choice.</h3><p>Leaders review outcome, adoption, cost, risk, and unresolved dependencies before funding the next increment.</p><strong>Gate evidence · outcome review</strong></li>
  </ol>

  <div class="tgs-footer">
    <p id="tgs-note"><strong>Accessible reading:</strong> the evidence list is authoritative. The line and circles above provide a visual route through the same five decisions.</p>
    <p class="tgs-legend"><span><i class="is-accent"></i>decision gate</span><span><i class="is-paper"></i>service evidence</span></p>
  </div>
</figure>

